WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.840
So if we're taking a look at the code that we have right now,

00:02.840 --> 00:05.760
you'll notice that if you checked out the 09-begin branch,

00:05.760 --> 00:08.440
you'll notice there's a new project in here called Say Love You.

00:08.440 --> 00:10.040
So for those not familiar with the friends,

00:10.040 --> 00:11.560
Say Love You just mean that it's life,

00:11.560 --> 00:13.960
this is life and so this is view.

00:13.960 --> 00:15.720
So inside of here,

00:15.720 --> 00:17.620
we actually do have a little bit happening here.

00:17.620 --> 00:20.200
So I do want to walk through this with you because I will try to

00:20.200 --> 00:23.640
sort of centralize the exercises around Say Love You in

00:23.640 --> 00:26.740
order to just provide some context and basically give you

00:26.740 --> 00:28.160
the experience of walking into a project that

00:28.160 --> 00:31.160
either has already had some call it legacy code,

00:31.160 --> 00:32.960
and that way you feel like you're working with stuff.

00:32.960 --> 00:35.360
But that said, I want to emphasize,

00:35.360 --> 00:36.880
if you feel more comfortable just working with

00:36.880 --> 00:39.380
your TV show forum app to apply these concepts,

00:39.380 --> 00:40.640
please feel free to do so.

00:40.640 --> 00:42.800
I just wanted to provide different context to allow you

00:42.800 --> 00:46.440
that practice of seeing what it's like when working with code bases.

00:46.440 --> 00:50.880
So let's go and switch over in here real quick into Say Love You.

00:50.880 --> 00:53.880
Let's go ahead and run that.

00:53.960 --> 00:58.080
NPM run dev, great.

00:58.080 --> 01:01.080
Now if we open up here.

01:01.440 --> 01:03.880
Oh, it's on 7.4 now.

01:03.880 --> 01:06.120
Oh, that's right, because the other one is running, in a sense.

01:06.120 --> 01:08.920
Okay. Here we go. We have Say Love You.

01:08.920 --> 01:10.760
It's a fairly simple app,

01:10.760 --> 01:12.280
but it has a little bit of styling this time,

01:12.280 --> 01:14.840
so not just raw HTML and whatever the browser provides.

01:14.840 --> 01:18.640
We have a home and login page or at least what appears to be.

01:18.640 --> 01:20.500
If we take a look at our app.view,

01:20.500 --> 01:23.200
you'll notice that there are two components that are

01:23.200 --> 01:24.400
already pre-built for you.

01:24.400 --> 01:26.600
There's a home page and a login page.

01:26.600 --> 01:28.440
If you look inside a package.json,

01:28.440 --> 01:30.680
you'll see there's still no router library.

01:30.680 --> 01:33.480
So there's no path being changed or anything right now.

01:33.480 --> 01:35.120
What we're doing here is that

01:35.120 --> 01:37.040
traditional single-page application model,

01:37.040 --> 01:40.040
which is like every JavaScript trying to manage everything,

01:40.040 --> 01:42.040
and so it's just routed there.

01:42.040 --> 01:44.240
So what's actually happening here is you have

01:44.240 --> 01:45.600
this reactive data that's tracking

01:45.600 --> 01:49.320
which the state of the current page, quote unquote.

01:49.320 --> 01:51.800
So here we have two methods that assign

01:51.800 --> 01:53.600
the current page to home or login,

01:53.600 --> 01:56.160
and then down here, we have the ability to say,

01:56.160 --> 01:59.000
okay, well, if the current page is home, show this component.

01:59.000 --> 02:00.520
If it's the login page,

02:00.520 --> 02:03.040
show or if current page is login,

02:03.040 --> 02:04.720
or actually in this case, it's in else.

02:04.720 --> 02:06.680
But as you can see, that's like your basic check

02:06.680 --> 02:08.160
to see what we're swapping between.

02:08.160 --> 02:09.880
Now here's the cool thing.

02:09.880 --> 02:12.200
This right here is great,

02:12.200 --> 02:14.560
but you can imagine that that list gets long.

02:14.560 --> 02:16.000
Again, for routing eventually,

02:16.000 --> 02:17.040
we're going to get into the library that allows

02:17.040 --> 02:18.520
to teach you how to switch routes.

02:18.520 --> 02:20.800
But if you have a list of components that you might

02:20.800 --> 02:22.920
need to swap in and out and make it dynamic,

02:22.920 --> 02:24.920
it's hard to have that all

02:24.920 --> 02:26.520
manage out inside of your templates, right?

02:26.520 --> 02:28.640
Either the conditionals, we get complicated,

02:28.640 --> 02:29.920
how would that actually work?

02:29.920 --> 02:32.140
So when it comes to dynamically swapping out components,

02:32.140 --> 02:35.160
Vue has a native component aptly called component.

02:35.160 --> 02:37.120
Because what you're doing is you're basically defining

02:37.120 --> 02:38.560
a generic component that

02:38.560 --> 02:42.080
JavaScript will basically help to define.

02:42.080 --> 02:45.000
So in the case of our app, for example,

02:45.000 --> 02:47.260
what we do is we pass it a prop called is,

02:47.260 --> 02:48.960
and this is a specially designed prop for

02:48.960 --> 02:50.880
the native component.

02:50.880 --> 02:53.080
So if we just do it manually ourselves,

02:53.080 --> 02:54.840
we can say, basically, we can say,

02:54.840 --> 02:56.920
oh, we're going to the home page.

02:56.920 --> 02:58.120
So in this particular case,

02:58.120 --> 03:01.000
you'll notice that home is

03:01.000 --> 03:03.600
basically being bound to just like a plane string,

03:03.600 --> 03:04.960
and there's nothing special going on.

03:04.960 --> 03:05.920
So if we think about it,

03:05.920 --> 03:07.760
this is really no difference than just

03:07.760 --> 03:11.320
declaring your home page directly as a component,

03:11.320 --> 03:12.640
like rendering out on the screen.

03:12.640 --> 03:15.800
But what we'd like to do is actually make it

03:15.800 --> 03:18.160
something that is managed via JavaScript.

03:18.360 --> 03:20.040
So what we could do in this particular case,

03:20.040 --> 03:21.960
is we can say, you know what, let's do this.

03:21.960 --> 03:27.880
Let's create a computed property and we'll call it,

03:27.880 --> 03:31.280
and this time, this one is called current page,

03:31.280 --> 03:33.960
and then we'll say render page.

03:33.960 --> 03:35.600
The way render page will work,

03:35.600 --> 03:40.800
we'll say is actually, yes, this is how to work.

03:40.800 --> 03:45.320
Return this.currentPage plus whatever.

03:45.320 --> 03:46.800
So basically, we're looking at the naming of

03:46.800 --> 03:48.920
the component here, in this case, it's home page,

03:48.920 --> 03:51.520
and so we can see now that because, whoops,

03:51.520 --> 03:54.800
let me go back. We can see now because we're

03:54.800 --> 03:56.720
only basically having the current page

03:56.720 --> 03:58.440
defined via the first part of it,

03:58.440 --> 04:00.520
via home and login,

04:00.520 --> 04:03.120
this means that we can basically tag it onto page,

04:03.120 --> 04:04.720
and if we save that now,

04:04.720 --> 04:07.920
do-do, yep, that's totally fine,

04:07.920 --> 04:12.480
and then bind this to render page.

04:12.480 --> 04:15.280
That's good, there you go.

04:15.320 --> 04:17.440
That's swapping in and out now.

04:17.440 --> 04:20.160
So what's really cool about this now is that you basically get

04:20.160 --> 04:22.920
the ability to do some pretty complex logic things,

04:22.920 --> 04:24.640
and then more importantly,

04:24.640 --> 04:26.880
you can actually start then when it comes to

04:26.880 --> 04:29.880
really making your application dynamic and having the backend

04:29.880 --> 04:31.800
define maybe which components your users

04:31.800 --> 04:33.040
prefer because you're managing

04:33.040 --> 04:35.400
a CMS site that might render out certain widgets.

04:35.400 --> 04:38.680
You might actually then do a loop through your V4 or,

04:38.680 --> 04:41.000
there's a bunch of things that you end up being able to do with this,

04:41.000 --> 04:43.320
but it's something I just wanted to expose to you all

04:43.320 --> 04:44.600
because as we go through,

04:44.600 --> 04:46.760
this concept is actually going to show up again

04:46.760 --> 04:49.640
as we go through things like routing.

